      "raw_exact_value": "A stationary wall cannot exhibit subject motion blur. The sole change affecting the wall between the two shots was switching from a tripod to handholding at a slower shutter speed. Camera shake during 1/60 s moved the entire image across the sensor, blurring every element—stationary and moving—uniformly. The decisive clue is that the object has no motion of its own, so the blur must originate from the camera's movement.",
