      "raw_exact_value": "Because the wall is motionless, its blur cannot come from subject motion. Removing the tripod introduced camera shake, and at 1/60 s the exposure lasted long enough for hand movement to shift the image across the sensor, producing blur on all scene elements—including the stationary wall. This matches the source principle that longer durations record more motion; here the relevant motion is the camera's own.",
